Create a new file src/web/types.ts that defines all shared types for the web server and frontend WebSocket communication. This file must NOT import from any other src/web/ file (it is the foundation). It may import from ../core/types.js for WorkflowPhase.

Define and export the following types:

1. LogEntry - A single entry in an agent log window: { id: string, timestamp: string, type: 'text' | 'thinking' | 'tool_call_start' | 'tool_call_end' | 'decision' | 'error', content: string, metadata?: Record<string, unknown> }

2. AgentWindowState - State of a single agent window: { agentId: string, profile: string, taskId?: string, active: boolean, log: LogEntry[] }

3. SidebarInfo - Workflow sidebar metadata: { title: string, indicator: string }

4. WorkflowSummary - Lightweight summary for sidebar list: { id: string, workflowName: string, status: 'running' | 'completed' | 'failed', sidebar: SidebarInfo, startedAt: string, completedAt?: string }

5. ServerMessage - Discriminated union of all server-to-client WS messages. Each variant has a type field and relevant data:
   - { type: 'init', workflows: WorkflowSummary[] }
   - { type: 'workflow_started', summary: WorkflowSummary }
   - { type: 'workflow_sidebar', workflowId: string, sidebar: SidebarInfo }
   - { type: 'workflow_phase', workflowId: string, phase: string, completed: string[] }
   - { type: 'workflow_state', workflowId: string, state: unknown }
   - { type: 'workflow_complete', workflowId: string, durationMs: number }
   - { type: 'workflow_failed', workflowId: string, error: string, phase: string }
   - { type: 'agent_spawned', workflowId: string, agent: AgentWindowState }
   - { type: 'agent_log', workflowId: string, agentId: string, entry: LogEntry }
   - { type: 'agent_complete', workflowId: string, agentId: string }

6. ClientMessage - Discriminated union of client-to-server messages:
   - { type: 'start_workflow', workflowName: string, taskPrompt: string, maxConcurrent?: number }
   - { type: 'select_workflow', workflowId: string }

7. WebServerOptions - Server config: { host: string, port: number, cwd: string }

Use TypeScript interfaces and type unions. Export all types. Use ESM syntax.

